<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Info</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> info
 info roots
 info &lt;category&gt;
 info &lt;ability, skill, spell or weapon&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre> info
 info roots
 info cat sword
 info dagger
 info strength
</pre>
<p>Use <b>info</b> at a teacher, before you <a cmd='help #'>practice</a>. It lists what that
teacher teaches you, the cheapest first, and what your next practice of each costs you.
Away from a teacher it doesn't work: <a cmd='#'>status</a> shows how good you are, but not
the costs.
</p>
<p>A line looks like this:
</p>
<pre>  32% dagger               [practice points   8] *
</pre>
<p>You have 32% in dagger, and practicing it once more now costs you 8 practice points.
The * means you've practiced it once already this level; each * makes the next practice
cost half as much again. What you pay depends on your own race and profession, so two
players can see different prices for the same thing.
</p>
<p>Other things you may see instead of the price:
</p>
<ul><li><b>[Practice next level]</b>: you can't practice it again this level.</li>
<li><b>[Teacher at max (80%). You are at 80% of your potential 105%]</b>: this teacher can't
take you further; find a teacher who can.</li>
<li><b>[REQ: Guild level:12 ]</b>: you need that guild level (or the level, or ability, shown)
first.</li>
<li>A name with nothing after it is a category (such as sword or axe hammer): <b>info
&lt;category&gt;</b> lists what's in it, <b>info roots</b> lists the categories.</li></ul>
<p>The list leaves out anything that would cost you more than 25 points. To see everything,
with your potential and the money a practice costs, use <a cmd='help #'>expert</a> mode.
</p>
<p>The best way to spend your points: practice each thing <b>once per level</b>, while it's
at its cheapest, and practice before you raise a <a cmd='help #'>level</a>, because
levelling starts the count again.
</p>
<p><br />
See also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Practice</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Expert</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Level</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Status</a>
</pre></div>
